course: dictionary
lesson: 12800
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them give the clues that show which meaning you need. Read the sentence, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «The elements of a story are its characters, setting, plot and problem.» Here elements means the parts that make something up. You can check by swapping in "parts": the parts of a story are its characters, setting, plot and problem. That makes sense.
explain: «The hikers were exposed to the elements all night.» Exposed to the elements means out in wind, rain and cold with no shelter. Here elements means the weather, not parts of anything.
fact: Elements can mean the parts or features that make up something.
fact: In science, an element is a pure substance made of one kind of atom, such as hydrogen or carbon.
fact: «The elements» means the weather, especially wind, rain and cold.
fact: «Braving the elements» means going out into bad weather even though it is harsh.
exercise: «The elements of a story are the characters, setting, plot and problem.» In this sentence, what does elements mean? | A noisy group of people in a crowd | A kind of chemical that cannot be split | *The parts that make up a story | The weather outside
exercise: «The hikers were exposed to the elements all night.» What does this mean? | Sleeping in a soft bed at home | Lost in a shopping centre | Locked safely inside a warm hut | *Out in the wind, rain and cold with no shelter
exercise: Hydrogen and carbon are examples of what? | Groups of people | Weather | *Elements | Stories
test: «The teacher explained the elements of grammar, starting with nouns and verbs.» What does elements mean here? | A kind of weather | Pictures in the book | *The basic, simple first parts of the subject | Long, difficult sentences
test: «She braved the elements to reach the school bus in the storm.» What does braved the elements mean? | Stayed at home in bed | Played a game with the storm | *Went out into harsh weather anyway | Sheltered under a bridge
exam: In science, what is an element? | A group of people in a crowd | *A pure substance made of one kind of atom | A story with a plot | Any kind of weather
